            <tr><td>Approve Requests</td><td>No</td><td>Yes</td><td>No</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Approve Lawyers</td><td>Yes</td><td>No</td><td>No</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Search Lawyers</td><td>No</td><td>No</td><td>Yes</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Profile Management</td><td>Yes</td><td>Yes</td><td>Yes</td></tr>
        </tbody>
    </table>

    <div class="page-break"></div>

    <h2>10. Software Requirements</h2>
    <ul>
        <li><strong>HTML/CSS:</strong> Structure and custom styling.</li>
        <li><strong>JavaScript:</strong> Client-side interactivity and form validations.</li>
        <li><strong>PHP:</strong> Server-side logic and application processing.</li>
        <li><strong>MySQL:</strong> Relational database management system.</li>
        <li><strong>XAMPP:</strong> Local development server (Apache + MySQL + PHP).</li>
        <li><strong>Bootstrap:</strong> Responsive front-end component framework.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>11. Hardware Requirements</h2>
    <table>
        <tbody>
            <tr><td><strong>Processor</strong></td><td>Dual-Core 2.0 GHz or higher</td></tr>
            <tr><td><strong>RAM</strong></td><td>4 GB (8 GB recommended)</td></tr>
            <tr><td><strong>Storage</strong></td><td>2 GB of free disk space</td></tr>
            <tr><td><strong>Display</strong></td><td>1366 x 768 resolution or higher</td></tr>
        </tbody>
    </table>

    <h2>12. Database Design</h2>
    <p>The LexElite system uses a relational MySQL database connecting tables for administrators, lawyers, customers, services, and appointments through foreign key relationships. The appointments table acts as the central link between clients and lawyers.</p>

    <h2>13. System Architecture</h2>
    <p>LexElite follows a traditional three-tier web application architecture:</p>
    <ul>
        <li><strong>Presentation Layer:</strong> Built using HTML, CSS, Bootstrap, and JS to render responsive interfaces.</li>
        <li><strong>Application Layer:</strong> Implemented in procedural PHP to handle business logic, session-based authentication, and role-based access control.</li>
        <li><strong>Data Layer:</strong> A MySQL relational database storing all persistent data securely.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>14. Project Workflow</h2>
    <ol>
        <li>Lawyer / Customer Registration</li>
        <li>Admin Reviews & Approves Lawyer</li>
        <li>Customer Logs In & Searches for Lawyers</li>
        <li>Customer Books an Appointment</li>
        <li>Lawyer Reviews & Approves / Rejects Request</li>
        <li>Customer Views Appointment Status</li>
    </ol>

    <div class="page-break"></div>

    <h2>15. User Interface</h2>
    <p><em>(Screenshots of the application interfaces such as Home Page, About Page, Admin Dashboard, Lawyer Dashboard, Customer Dashboard, Login/Registration forms, and Appointment Booking screens are to be inserted here.)</em></p>

    <h2>16. Key Modules</h2>
    <ul>
        <li><strong>Admin Module:</strong> The control center granting full authority over lawyer approval, client oversight, and reporting.</li>
        <li><strong>Lawyer Module:</strong> Equips attorneys with tools to manage their daily interactions, review appointment requests, and maintain an up-to-date profile.</li>
        <li><strong>Customer Module:</strong> The primary point of interaction for end users to discover lawyers, book appointments, and track consultation history.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>17. Database Tables</h2>
    <ul>
        <li><strong>admin:</strong> Stores administrator login credentials.</li>
        <li><strong>lawyers:</strong> Stores lawyer registration details, category, profile image, and approval status (Pending/Approved/Rejected).</li>
        <li><strong>customers:</strong> Stores client registration details, contact info, and passwords.</li>
        <li><strong>appointments:</strong> The central booking table linking a customer and lawyer together with an appointment date, time, and status.</li>
        <li><strong>services:</strong> Stores the legal categories and specialized services offered on the platform.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>18. Advantages</h2>
    <ul>
        <li>Centralized platform connecting clients, lawyers, and administrators.</li>
        <li>Eliminates manual, paper-based appointment booking.</li>
        <li>Gives clients permanent, digital access to their booking history.</li>
        <li>Ensures only verified, admin-approved lawyers are visible to clients.</li>
        <li>Fully responsive design ensures accessibility across devices.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>19. Testing</h2>
    <p>The system was manually tested across all three panels. Key test cases include:</p>
    <ul>
        <li><strong>Admin Login:</strong> Redirects to Admin Dashboard on valid credentials. (Passed)</li>
        <li><strong>Lawyer Registration:</strong> New lawyer saved with Pending status. (Passed)</li>
        <li><strong>Lawyer Approval:</strong> Admin can approve/reject a lawyer. (Passed)</li>
        <li><strong>Book Appointment:</strong> Customer appointment created with Pending status. (Passed)</li>
        <li><strong>Approve Request:</strong> Lawyer can update appointment status. (Passed)</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>20. Conclusion</h2>
    <p>The LexElite system successfully demonstrates how a structured web application can digitize and simplify legal consultations. By connecting clients, lawyers, and administrators, the system reduces friction from lawyer discovery to appointment booking. Built with PHP and MySQL, it provides a solid foundation for secure, transparent legal networking.</p>

